cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or cite the exploratory study, please use the metadata below (update DOI after Zenodo release)."
title: "Green-Channel CLAHE and a Mild-Weighted Threshold Objective for Cross-Dataset Diabetic Retinopathy Grading with MobileViT-S: An Exploratory Evaluation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ishaq
    given-names: Zubair Md
    email: zubairishaq12@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent researcher
abstract: >-
  Exploratory APTOS-only MobileViT-S evaluation of RGB versus green-channel CLAHE
  and cross-entropy versus a mild-weighted shared-weight threshold objective, with
  external testing on IDRiD, Messidor-2 and DeepDRiD. Results are schedule-stratified
  (seeds 42-44 truncated LR versus 45-47 full cosine). Threshold-head outputs were
  non-monotonic; calibration is reported only for cross-entropy models.
version: 1.0.0-exploratory
license: MIT
